1
00:00:06,225 --> 00:00:10,045
Last time, we asked: a plastic box, a metal box and a

2
00:00:09,795 --> 00:00:10,845
glass jar.

3
00:00:11,135 --> 00:00:13,205
One of them was made from sand!

4
00:00:13,495 --> 00:00:14,425
Which one?

5
00:00:14,553 --> 00:00:16,233
We have sorted living things.

6
00:00:16,513 --> 00:00:18,163
Now, non-living things.

7
00:00:18,433 --> 00:00:19,753
What are they made of?

8
00:00:20,024 --> 00:00:21,354
A plastic box.

9
00:00:21,634 --> 00:00:22,854
A metal box.

10
00:00:23,134 --> 00:00:24,244
A glass jar.

11
00:00:24,504 --> 00:00:26,084
Did you lock in your answer?

12
00:00:28,235 --> 00:00:29,695
You against the Buddies!

13
00:00:29,965 --> 00:00:31,195
Lock in first.

14
00:00:31,465 --> 00:00:33,285
One finger for every point.

15
00:00:33,565 --> 00:00:35,865
A little sparrow is hiding in this video.

16
00:00:36,165 --> 00:00:37,355
Can you spot it?

17
00:00:37,935 --> 00:00:39,265
Today you'll learn:

18
00:00:39,463 --> 00:00:41,203
Objects and materials.

19
00:00:41,402 --> 00:00:43,282
Four of the seven materials.

20
00:00:43,485 --> 00:00:45,115
Where each one comes from.

21
00:00:45,766 --> 00:00:46,706
Are you ready?

22
00:00:47,146 --> 00:00:47,916
Three!

23
00:00:48,296 --> 00:00:48,956
Two!

24
00:00:49,326 --> 00:00:49,976
One!

25
00:00:50,396 --> 00:00:51,116
Go!

26
00:00:51,545 --> 00:00:52,785
Look at this spoon.

27
00:00:53,055 --> 00:00:55,905
A spoon is an object: a thing you use.

28
00:00:56,419 --> 00:00:57,689
What is it made of?

29
00:00:57,969 --> 00:00:58,769
Metal!

30
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:00,859
Metal is its material.

31
00:01:02,369 --> 00:01:03,599
Say it with me!

32
00:01:04,313 --> 00:01:06,583
Materials are used to make objects.

33
00:01:06,763 --> 00:01:09,723
Objects are things you use for different purposes.

34
00:01:13,526 --> 00:01:14,276
My rule!

35
00:01:14,466 --> 00:01:16,006
A window is made of glass.

36
00:01:16,086 --> 00:01:17,656
So a window is a material!

37
00:01:17,933 --> 00:01:19,493
Something is not right.

38
00:01:19,763 --> 00:01:21,943
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

39
00:01:22,223 --> 00:01:23,183
Hold on!

40
00:01:28,696 --> 00:01:29,826
Arms crossed?

41
00:01:30,096 --> 00:01:31,256
One finger up!

42
00:01:31,546 --> 00:01:33,026
Glass is the material.

43
00:01:33,286 --> 00:01:35,016
The window is the object.

44
00:01:35,377 --> 00:01:36,047
Oops!

45
00:01:36,157 --> 00:01:37,407
Window: object.

46
00:01:37,447 --> 00:01:38,707
Glass: material!

47
00:01:40,095 --> 00:01:40,975
Round one.

48
00:01:41,285 --> 00:01:43,025
Which one was made from sand?

49
00:01:43,295 --> 00:01:45,015
One, the plastic box.

50
00:01:45,285 --> 00:01:46,795
Two, the metal box.

51
00:01:47,055 --> 00:01:48,585
Three, the glass jar.

52
00:01:48,875 --> 00:01:50,355
Show me with your fingers.

53
00:01:55,822 --> 00:01:56,802
Locked in!

54
00:01:56,930 --> 00:01:57,670
Two!

55
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,500
Metal comes from the ground.

56
00:01:59,570 --> 00:02:00,820
So does sand!

57
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:01,331
Three.

58
00:02:01,931 --> 00:02:04,041
Sand has tiny clear grains.

59
00:02:04,093 --> 00:02:04,833
Three!

60
00:02:04,933 --> 00:02:06,583
Very hot sand can melt.

61
00:02:06,643 --> 00:02:08,533
Like ice cream, but much hotter!

62
00:02:09,037 --> 00:02:10,387
Be a grain of sand!

63
00:02:10,677 --> 00:02:11,667
Shrink down.

64
00:02:11,947 --> 00:02:12,877
Quietly.

65
00:02:15,163 --> 00:02:18,493
You are a grain of sand, in a huge pile of sand.

66
00:02:19,164 --> 00:02:20,654
A big scoop lifts you.

67
00:02:21,444 --> 00:02:24,474
You slide into a furnace, a very hot oven.

68
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:26,920
You get hotter, and hotter.

69
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:29,760
You melt into a glowing liquid!

70
00:02:30,422 --> 00:02:33,602
You are poured into a mould, in the shape of a jar.

71
00:02:34,267 --> 00:02:35,427
You cool down.

72
00:02:36,207 --> 00:02:37,477
You are hard again.

73
00:02:38,317 --> 00:02:39,927
And now, you are clear.

74
00:02:40,587 --> 00:02:41,717
You are glass.

75
00:02:44,134 --> 00:02:45,494
The answer is three.

76
00:02:45,774 --> 00:02:46,974
The glass jar!

77
00:02:47,325 --> 00:02:48,455
Look closer.

78
00:02:48,845 --> 00:02:50,925
Here is the sand, in a furnace.

79
00:02:51,365 --> 00:02:52,165
Watch!

80
00:02:52,287 --> 00:02:56,067
When sand is heated until it is very hot, it melts and

81
00:02:55,817 --> 00:02:56,847
becomes clear.

82
00:02:59,010 --> 00:03:00,820
Glass is made from sand.

83
00:03:04,670 --> 00:03:05,760
Three fingers?

84
00:03:06,030 --> 00:03:07,240
One finger up!

85
00:03:08,515 --> 00:03:10,195
Look closer at this rock.

86
00:03:10,635 --> 00:03:11,705
Shiny bits!

87
00:03:12,085 --> 00:03:13,875
That is metal, in the rock.

88
00:03:14,005 --> 00:03:16,275
Metals can be dug up from the ground.

89
00:03:18,965 --> 00:03:23,895
Gold, iron, copper and aluminium are metals that are found naturally in

90
00:03:23,645 --> 00:03:24,465
the ground.

91
00:03:28,447 --> 00:03:29,577
Look closer.

92
00:03:29,967 --> 00:03:32,537
Dark, sticky oil goes into the factory.

93
00:03:32,897 --> 00:03:34,337
Plastic comes out!

94
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:39,050
Plastic is made in factories using oil that comes from deep under

95
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:39,650
the ground.

96
00:03:43,534 --> 00:03:45,024
My snack box was oil?

97
00:03:45,144 --> 00:03:47,694
Good thing my biscuits do not taste like oil!

98
00:03:49,081 --> 00:03:50,081
Round two.

99
00:03:50,371 --> 00:03:52,381
This noodle bowl is ceramic.

100
00:03:53,581 --> 00:03:55,221
What is ceramic made from?

101
00:03:55,521 --> 00:03:56,491
One, sand.

102
00:03:56,761 --> 00:03:57,701
Two, clay.

103
00:03:57,981 --> 00:03:58,961
Three, oil.

104
00:03:59,241 --> 00:04:00,721
Show me with your fingers.

105
00:04:06,192 --> 00:04:07,172
Locked in!

106
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:07,890
One.

107
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:09,180
Sand.

108
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:11,520
The bowl is smooth, like glass.

109
00:04:11,575 --> 00:04:12,385
Two!

110
00:04:12,425 --> 00:04:13,555
Not sand.

111
00:04:13,635 --> 00:04:15,075
Sand made the glass.

112
00:04:15,122 --> 00:04:15,752
Two!

113
00:04:15,882 --> 00:04:16,642
Clay!

114
00:04:16,712 --> 00:04:18,652
I made a clay pot in art class.

115
00:04:18,928 --> 00:04:20,228
The answer is two.

116
00:04:20,518 --> 00:04:21,298
Clay!

117
00:04:21,344 --> 00:04:24,254
Clay can be found in soil dug from the ground.

118
00:04:27,069 --> 00:04:28,309
The clay is shaped.

119
00:04:28,579 --> 00:04:31,689
Then it is baked in a very hot oven, called a kiln.

120
00:04:32,879 --> 00:04:34,009
Look closer.

121
00:04:34,389 --> 00:04:35,979
The clay bowl is soft.

122
00:04:36,339 --> 00:04:37,919
Into the kiln it goes!

123
00:04:38,131 --> 00:04:41,291
Heating hardens ceramic, but it can break easily.

124
00:04:43,603 --> 00:04:44,763
Say it with me!

125
00:04:45,471 --> 00:04:47,651
Ceramic is a material made from clay.

126
00:04:47,801 --> 00:04:49,321
Glass is made from sand.

127
00:04:52,533 --> 00:04:53,563
Two fingers?

128
00:04:53,833 --> 00:04:55,053
One finger up!

129
00:04:55,551 --> 00:04:57,011
Show me your score hand!

130
00:04:57,311 --> 00:04:58,381
Three fingers?

131
00:04:58,661 --> 00:04:59,661
High five!

132
00:05:00,313 --> 00:05:01,783
Did you spot the sparrow?

133
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:03,763
It was on the classroom window!

134
00:05:04,053 --> 00:05:06,043
What material is a window made of?

135
00:05:06,373 --> 00:05:07,673
Tell someone at home.

136
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,600
Let's read today's key words together!

137
00:05:10,890 --> 00:05:11,650
Ready?

138
00:05:11,987 --> 00:05:12,753
Object.

139
00:05:14,312 --> 00:05:15,111
Material.

140
00:05:16,662 --> 00:05:17,512
Ceramic.

141
00:05:18,909 --> 00:05:19,649
Clay.

142
00:05:20,887 --> 00:05:21,827
Well done!

143
00:05:22,824 --> 00:05:24,384
Three materials to go!

144
00:05:24,644 --> 00:05:26,674
The sole of your school shoe is rubber.

145
00:05:26,944 --> 00:05:29,154
Some rubber starts as white drops!

146
00:05:29,414 --> 00:05:30,984
Where do the drops come from?

147
00:05:31,264 --> 00:05:32,854
Find out in Part Two!

148
00:05:34,213 --> 00:05:35,314
Say it with us!

149
00:05:36,114 --> 00:05:36,864
Ready?

150
00:05:36,988 --> 00:05:37,648
One!

151
00:05:37,988 --> 00:05:38,688
two!

152
00:05:38,993 --> 00:05:40,168
Now you know!
